Grammar

    0 $accept: loop $end

    1 loop: S_1 S_2

    2 oneLine: expr

    3 expr: atom
    4      | expr `+` expr
    5      | expr `*` expr
    6      | expr `-` expr
    7      | expr `/` expr
    8      | `(` expr `)`

    9 atom: ID
   10      | LONG
   11      | DOUBLE
   12      | QUOTE

   13 S_1: ε
   14      | NL

   15 S_2_E: S_2_E NL oneLine
   16      | oneLine
   17      | S_2_E NL

   18 S_2: S_2_E


Terminals, with rules where they appear

    $end (0) 0
    error (256)
    `(` (258) 8
    `)` (259) 8
    LONG (260) 10
    DOUBLE (261) 11
    ID (262) 9
    QUOTE (263) 12
    NL (264) 14 15 17
    `+` (265) 4
    `-` (266) 6
    `*` (267) 5
    `/` (268) 7


Nonterminals, with rules where they appear

    $accept (14)
        on left: 0
    loop (15)
        on left: 1
        on right: 0
    oneLine (16)
        on left: 2
        on right: 15 16
    expr (17)
        on left: 3 4 5 6 7 8
        on right: 2 4 5 6 7 8
    atom (18)
        on left: 9 10 11 12
        on right: 3
    S_1 (19)
        on left: 13 14
        on right: 1
    S_2_E (20)
        on left: 15 16 17
        on right: 15 17 18
    S_2 (21)
        on left: 18
        on right: 1


State 0

    0 $accept: • loop $end

    NL  shift, and go to state 1

    $default  reduce using rule 13 (S_1)

    loop  go to state 2
    S_1  go to state 3


